the campground's entrance, and it's easily accessible for most RVs and trailers. The dump station is free for campers, but donations are appreciated to help maintain the facility.\\n\\n**Rules and Regulations**\\n\\nHere are some rules and regulations to keep in mind when using the potable water and dump station facilities:\\n\\n1. **Potable Water**: Potable water is available for campers to refill their RV's water tank. However, it's not meant for washing vehicles or equipment. Please be mindful of your water usage, as the campground relies on a limited water supply.\\n2. **Dump Station**: The dump station is for RV waste only. Do not dispose of trash, recyclables, or hazardous materials in the dump station. Make sure to follow proper dumping procedures to avoid clogging the system.\\n3. **Water Conservation**: Colter Bay Campground is located in a water-sensitive area, so please conserve water whenever possible. Take shorter showers, turn off the faucet while washing dishes, and report any leaks to the campground staff.\\n4. **Grey Water Disposal**: If you have a grey water tank, you can dispose of it at the dump station. However, make sure to follow the campground's guidelines for grey water disposal.\\n5. **Black Water Disposal**: Black water (sewage) must be disposed of at the dump station only. Do not dispose of black water in the campground's restrooms or showers.\\n\\n**Additional Tips**\\n\\n1. **Water Pressure**: The water pressure at the potable water stations can be high, so be prepared to use a pressure regulator to avoid damaging your RV's plumbing system.\\n2. **Dump Station Etiquette**: Be respectful of other campers when using the dump station. Try to avoid using the dump station during peak hours (usually around check-in and check-out times), and keep the area clean and tidy.\\n\\nBy following these rules and regulations, you'll help ensure a safe and enjoyable camping experience for yourself and others at Colter Bay Campground. \"}], 'Chat Time: 2